 144)<br>3. = √169 = 13"},{"text":"C(−3; −1) and D(1; 2)","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"CD","a":"5","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Use the distance formula.","steps":"1. Formula (distance): AB = √((x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²)<br>2. CD = √((1 − (−3))² + (2 − (−1))²) = √(4² + 3²)<br>3. = √(16 + 9) = √25 = 5"},{"text":"E(2; −3) and F(7; −3)","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"EF","a":"5","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Horizontal.","steps":"1. Formula (distance): AB = √((x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²)<br>2. EF = √((7 − 2)² + (−3 − (−3))²) = √(25 + 0)<br>3. = 5"}]}